    ('reading-rdl-31b26c1c58817872c3cb29f1', 'The article indicates which of the following about the event at Adler Auditorium? 23. The article indicates which of the following about the event at Adler Auditorium? It was covered by several media outlets. It centered on students pursuing the same degree. It was introduced by a professor of film studies. It was sponsored by a student organization. The article suggests that the four films 24. The article suggests that the four films showed different levels of technical proficiency featured students as actors were shot in black and white covered a range of emotional tones The article mentions each of the following EXCEPT 25. The article mentions each of the following EXCEPT other projects completed by the filmmakers the venue where the screenings were held the subject matter of each film that was shown the inspiration behind one of the films ON MARCH 18, FILM STUDIES MAJORS PRESENTED THEIR WORK AT
ADLER AUDITORIUM.
Four short films created by students were screened, and each
filmmaker answered questions from audience members. The films
were striking in their variety. The program began with a whimsical
animated film, Insides, depicting the internal organs of a human body
interacting with one another like family members. Filmmaker
Kat Morgan said the idea came to her while she was taking
Human Anatomy 101.
Next up was Alan Hinds'' sober black-and-white documentary
On My Feet, chronicling his brother''s unsuccessful attempt to become
a champion marathon runner.
The third film in the series was Margot Bridges'' comedy The Date,
about a mismatched couple on a movie date.
And lastly, the audience saw The Friend, Priti Patel''s tender depiction
of a toddler''s relationship with a protective dog.
All four films were technically accomplished, engaging, and reflective
of each filmmaker''s distinctive, individual talents.'),
