    ('reading-rdl-4e1dc8a89389627aca7cf10f', 'What is the main problem that Colin expresses about the assignment? 23. What is the main problem that Colin expresses about the assignment? He believes the topic is unimportant. He finds the topic too general to approach easily. He believes that the prompt makes false assumptions. He does not understand the assignment. What does Priya suggest is the purpose of the assignment? 24. What does Priya suggest is the purpose of the assignment? To summarize existing research on remote learning To criticize existing research on remote learning To choose a viewpoint and support it with arguments To analyze one''s personal experience with online courses What does Colin struggle with when reviewing the research? 25. What does Colin struggle with when reviewing the research? It discusses too many topics. It contradicts his own experience. It relies too heavily on theory. It is intended for experts only. Colin (8:20 P.M.):
I’m still wrestling with this week’s assignment. I get
it that we have to evaluate the longterm implications
of remote learning, but that feels incredibly broad.
Priya (8:22 P.M.):
I had the same reaction. I think the goal is to
show we can take a position and use evidence
to back it up, not cover every possible angle.
Mateo (8:26 P.M.):
Agreed. I’m focusing on how online courses affect
students’ motivation over time. There’s plenty of
research, but the findings contradict each other,
which makes the analysis tricky.
Colin (8:29 P.M.):
Exactly. Every article I read raises a
different concern—participation, cognitive
load, course design. It’s hard to figure out
which thread to prioritize.
Priya (8:31 P.M.):
I’d pick the one you can argue most clearly. The
professor said clarity matters more than trying to
sound "comprehensive."'),
    ('reading-rdl-4ec0fa96851b731790db9844', 'Based on the description, the course will most likely teach students to 21. Based on the description, the course will most likely teach students to curate museum collections authenticate works of art study historical objects analyze ancient poetry It can be inferred from the description that to fulfill course requirements the students must 22. It can be inferred from the description that to fulfill course requirements the students must discuss ancient art during class sessions share their findings with the museum staff sign up to volunteer at the National Museum submit a number of written assignments ANTR 201
