    ('reading-rdl-5dded3a998e1aa70151d92c3', 'All of the following are mentioned as features of the EcoHousing initiative EXCEPT 28. All of the following are mentioned as features of the EcoHousing initiative EXCEPT solar power composting bins shared gardening spaces the collection of rainwater According to the article, a survey revealed that a large percentage of Greenleaf students are 29. According to the article, a survey revealed that a large percentage of Greenleaf students are choosing to major in environmental science demanding more spacious rooms in dormitories seeking housing that is environmentally friendly dissatisfied with the university''s housing options Why does the article mention a discount? 30. Why does the article mention a discount? To suggest that housing fees have increased significantly To highlight that EcoHousing costs more than traditional dorms To encourage students to attend the recycling workshops To feature an incentive that the university offers to students The Rise of Sustainable Living
in University Housing
Martinsburg (April 10)
As universities trend toward eco-consciousness, more students
are embracing sustainable living in campus housing.
At Greenleaf University, the new EcoHousing initiative
features solar panels and rainwater-harvesting systems.
Select dorms also have communal gardens. This program
aligns with students’ growing demand for environmentally
friendly spaces.
In a recent survey, 78 percent of Greenleaf students expressed
interest in sustainable housing. The initiative also includes
workshops on recycling and energy conservation, aiming to
create environmentally aware graduates.
Emily Hart, a senior in environmental science, noted, “Living
sustainably on campus shows that daily choices have
global impact.” The administration hopes this program will
inspire other schools to follow suit.
Greenleaf even offers financial incentives: Students who
choose EcoHousing receive a 5 percent discount on housing
fees. The university plans to expand the initiative to more
dorms next year.'),
    ('reading-rdl-5de606d5f8a114ba9be15497', 'What is Momentum Meet-up primarily designed to help students do? 23. What is Momentum Meet-up primarily designed to help students do? Choose an academic major Get help writing their résumés Establish professional contacts Discover volunteer opportunities What are attendees asked to bring to the event? 24. What are attendees asked to bring to the event? At least 100 business cards Multiple copies of their résumé Money to pay for refreshments A name tag and discussion topics What should attendees do to receive tips about networking before the mixer? 25. What should attendees do to receive tips about networking before the mixer? Download a PDF document Join an online FAQ session Attend an orientation the day before Arrive at the event early Momentum Meet-up: Networking Mixer for Students
Build real-world connections with peers, alumni, and local employers
at our campus-wide mixer!
