    ('reading-rdl-602984a3fd83793f8d8ce5ed', 'Why does Angela recommend bringing a lot of water for the hike? 28. Why does Angela recommend bringing a lot of water for the hike? The trail will eventually climb to an extremely high altitude. The conditions along the trail will be exceptionally windy and dusty. The water for sale along the trail is too expensive. The temperature along the trail will start to climb after about nine a.m. At 5:30 P.M., what does Angela imply when she writes, “Let me check on that, Tom”? 29. At 5:30 P.M., what does Angela imply when she writes, “Let me check on that, Tom”? She knows that the hiking trails in Green Valley are not protected. She is concerned about the difficulty of the trail at Green Valley. She is unsure whether a permit is required for hiking on the trail. She knows that a permit is not required for parking. What does Milton offer to do? 30. What does Milton offer to do? Rent a car for the group Use his car for carpooling Bring extra water Use his home as a gathering place Angela Kim (5:00 p.m.)
Hi everyone! Want to join me for a hike on Saturday at Green Valley with
