    ('reading-rdl-618bf4056104c302387d73c6', 'Which of the following is most likely true of Discovering Human Cultures? 21. Which of the following is most likely true of Discovering Human Cultures? It includes guides for conducting research. The case studies it contains use fictitious names. The methodologies it uses are not conventional. It is being made into an informational television series. What is suggested about the writing style of Discovering Human Cultures? 22. What is suggested about the writing style of Discovering Human Cultures? Its language is ideal for advanced anthropology courses. It is written to be understood by general audiences. It often uses humor to make a point. Its use of non-English expressions adds authenticity. Discovering Human Cultures by Dr. R. J. Hancock explores
