    ('reading-rdl-67b206fb484942017750a06b', 'What is the main topic of the article? 23. What is the main topic of the article? A college campus is the backdrop of a Hollywood film. A graduating student is given a role in a Hollywood film. A film screening on campus draws a large crowd. A celebrated alumnus reconnects with his college. What did Daniel Rivero do at Ashburn? 24. What did Daniel Rivero do at Ashburn? He gave an interview to the student newspaper. He held auditions for his latest film. He taught an unscheduled acting class. He announced his role in an upcoming film. What is the meaning of Daniel Rivero’s advice to students? 25. What is the meaning of Daniel Rivero’s advice to students? Creative thinking begins when things go wrong. It is good to leave home, but come back often. Poor choices can stifle innovation if you are not careful. Dream big and do not let anyone stand in your way. Award Winner Returns to Alma Mater
By Kevin Martin
Students were stunned when actor Daniel Rivero, famous
for his award-winning role in Horizon''s Edge, visited
Ashburn College on Monday.
Rivero, a recent graduate of the Theater Arts program,
returned to lead an impromptu drama workshop. Students
crowded the theater hall, snapping selfies with the star and
asking about his journey from Ashburn to Hollywood.
"I skipped lunch just to hear him," said sophomore
Lily Chen. Rivero shared stories from his early auditions,
including moments of rejection that taught him resilience.
"Embrace failure—it''s the doorway to invention," he told
students. He also praised Ashburn''s faculty for fostering his
love of storytelling. "It feels like I never left," he added.
The visit sparked excitement across campus, with social
media flooded by photos from the workshop. For many
students, it was a reminder that big dreams can start
in small classrooms.'),
