    ('reading-rdl-70dd2b5537ed5b6a71a0d0fc', 'What is the main topic of the article? 23. What is the main topic of the article? A debate among campus baristas over coffee-making methods How students are learning robotics in class A technological innovation at the campus café A plan to open an automated drive-through café on campus What is indicated about the robot baristas? 24. What is indicated about the robot baristas? They are meant to make drink service faster. They are not yet able to create latte art. They require cash payments for all orders. They were designed by engineering students. What is indicated about student reactions to the new baristas? 25. What is indicated about student reactions to the new baristas? Students are worried that the quality of the coffee will decline. Students are afraid that robots will soon replace professors. Most students are annoyed at the increase in prices necessitated by the cost of the new baristas. Some students find the idea amusing and novel, while others object to it on principle. The campus café launched two AI-powered
robot baristas this week, aiming to reduce wait
times during peak hours. Each robot can brew
50 drinks per hour and accepts mobile payments
only. The $100,000 investment was funded by a
tech grant. Students can customize drinks via an
app, which even allows them to choose latte art
generated by algorithms.
The robots are stationed in two high-traffic spots: one inside the
main student center and the other in the engineering building’s
atrium. These locations were chosen to serve both social spaces and
academic hubs where coffee demand is highest.
“We’re blending convenience with innovation,” said campus café
manager Jordan Lee.
“It’s about creating a futuristic experience.” “I ordered a cappuccino,
and the foam had a smiley face,” said junior Maya Patel. “It’s weird
but fun.”
On launch day, a small group of students protested the replacement
of student workers with robots.'),
    ('reading-rdl-72408ea6914bc556a20ce824', 'What is the main topic of the article? 23. What is the main topic of the article? A new energy-saving initiative A community''s resilience during a disruption A musical event on campus An announcement about a technology upgrade What is indicated about the outage? 24. What is indicated about the outage? It led to the cancellation of final exams. It was planned for routine maintenance. It was caused by an equipment failure. It was limited to a single dormitory. How might student behavior during the blackout be best described? 25. How might student behavior during the blackout be best described? They largely abandoned their studies. They found creative solutions and even enjoyed themselves. They posted angry comments on social media. They left campus in large numbers. Blackout Brings
Creativity to Finals Week
A sudden power outage during finals week left Smithfield
students scrambling for solutions. Students took advantage
of their smart-phone flashlights, and university staff provided
camping lights for dorm lounges.
"It was stressful but kind of fun," said sophomore Grace Lee.
The blackout lasted six hours, caused by a transformer failure
near campus. Dining services offered free coffee, and
professors extended deadlines to ease the pressure.
"We made the best of it," said senior Omar Davis, who
studied with his bike light. Social media buzzed with photos
of candlelit study sessions, turning the inconvenience into a
moment of campus unity.
Some students even organized impromptu acoustic concerts
on the quad, proving that creativity thrives under constraints.
"It reminded us that community matters more than
convenience," said Professor Laura Chen.
By the early morning hours, power was restored, but the
evening''s events left a lasting impression.'),
    ('reading-rdl-75ae12fd735b71b1b761a4d6', 'Who is Sandeep going to the concert with? 25. Who is Sandeep going to the concert with? His cousin His classmate Fatima His friend How does Sandeep most likely feel about Fatima’s situation? 26. How does Sandeep most likely feel about Fatima’s situation? Happy Relieved Indifferent Disappointed At 10:05 A.M., what does Fatima most likely mean when she writes, “I would like to, but one of my classmates has been out sick all week and our report is due tomorrow”? 27. At 10:05 A.M., what does Fatima most likely mean when she writes, “I would like to, but one of my classmates has been out sick all week and our report is due tomorrow”? She feels too ill to go to the concert. She will take next week off from work. She does not think the concert will be enjoyable. She is unlikely to be able to attend the concert. Sandeep Patel (10:00 A.M.)
