    ('reading-rdl-98e360bf3b87450aaef50862', 'What is the notice primarily about? 25. What is the notice primarily about? Providing safety tips during a storm Announcing a disruption to a service Providing after-installation instructions for a new appliance Promoting a community water park opening What should residents do beforehand? 26. What should residents do beforehand? Plan for power outages Disconnect all water appliances Inspect faucets and showers for leaks Ensure enough water is stored for one day What can be inferred about the event described in the announcement? 27. What can be inferred about the event described in the announcement? It can be postponed to a different day by calling the maintenance department. It is required for infrastructure upgrades. It will occur weekly. It is due to a natural disaster. Attention Residents!
Due to necessary maintenance on the main water line, there will be a
temporary interruption in water service for all residents in the Maplewood
dormitory.
Date: Monday, March 15 Time: 9:00 A.M.- 4:00 P.M.
Important Information:
1.Preparation:
• Fill containers with water for drinking and cooking before the interruption.
• Store enough water for personal hygiene needs.
2.During the Interruption:
• Do not attempt to use faucets, showers, or any appliances that require
water.
• Toilets may not function properly; please plan accordingly.
3.After Service Resumes:
• Run cold water through all faucets for a few minutes to clear any sediment.
• Check for any leaks and report them immediately to the maintenance
department.
Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact the
Maplewood Maintenance Department at 555-4321.
We apologize for the inconvenience and appreciate your understanding as
we work to improve our community''s water infrastructure.'),
