    ('reading-rdl-a4e03a07341ab5f033400562', 'What is the nature of the problem Marcus reports? 25. What is the nature of the problem Marcus reports? A maintenance issue A financial shortfall A personal dispute An academic difficulty Which of the following solutions does Marcus prefer, according to the email? 26. Which of the following solutions does Marcus prefer, according to the email? A permanent move to another room Talking things over with a third party Monetary compensation A temporary switch to off-campus housing Which of the following best describes the overall tone of the email? 27. Which of the following best describes the overall tone of the email? Angry Apologetic Uncompromising Reasonable To:
housing@prairieu.edu
From:
mlee20@prairieu.edu
Sent:
October 25, 2025, 8:12 P.M.
Subject:
Mediation options
Dear Housing Office,
I’m writing about ongoing tension with my roommate in Matthis Hall,
Room 318. We disagree on quiet hours and guests, and lately our
conversations have started feeling heated. We tried setting a schedule,
but it hasn’t stuck. I don’t want this to escalate, and I’d prefer a solution
that keeps us both in the room.
Could you explain the mediation process? Do you offer conflict
resolution sessions with a resident advisor or professional staff, and
are meeting notes kept confidential? If we need a temporary room
change during exams, how does that work?
I’m available most weekdays after 4 P.M. I appreciate the work your
team does to support a healthy living environment, and I want to
resolve this respectfully.
Thank you,
Marcus Lee'),
    ('reading-rdl-a88ed88421140037bf706c10', 'What is the main purpose of the email? 28. What is the main purpose of the email? To confirm attendance at a lecture for academic credit To apply for a research assistant position at a policy institute To request a letter of recommendation for a job in the energy sector To arrange a conversation about an expert''s professional experience What aspect of energy regulation is Serena interested in? 29. What aspect of energy regulation is Serena interested in? Its ability to solve the energy industry''s problems Its relation to markets Its critique of traditional fuels Its effects on building new energy infrastructure What will Serena probably do if Ms. Thomas offers to call her on a Tuesday morning? 30. What will Serena probably do if Ms. Thomas offers to call her on a Tuesday morning? Remind her that she is free on Monday and Wednesday afternoons Suggest that they have the call on the weekend instead Change her own schedule and agree to a call on Tuesday Suggest that they compromise and speak on a Monday or Wednesday morning To:
