    ('reading-rdl-ad6e5c3587f5a63bb2d6563f', 'What is indicated about the skills students will develop from taking the CULN 310 course? 28. What is indicated about the skills students will develop from taking the CULN 310 course? They will gain expertise in general culinary management techniques. They will become proficient in the use of a technically complex cooking technique. They will learn to critique historical culinary trends as restaurant critics. They will become experts in the practical applications of plant-based ingredients. What is indicated about the eligibility criteria for enrolling in CULN 310? 29. What is indicated about the eligibility criteria for enrolling in CULN 310? Enrollment is open to all students with an interest in gastronomic science. Admission requires an advanced understanding of the sous vide technique. Candidates must have completed two introductory courses in the department. Students are required to possess prior work experience in an industrial kitchen. Which aspect of sous vide does the syllabus suggest will be a significant component of the course? 30. Which aspect of sous vide does the syllabus suggest will be a significant component of the course? The financial implications of sous vide in restaurant operations The cultural influences on the evolution of sous vide The technological development of sous vide techniques over time The ethical considerations of using sous vide techniques Global Culinary Institute
Spring 2024
CULN 310 Advanced Techniques: Sous Vide
Course Description: This course explores the sous vide culinary
method, a meticulous process in which vacuum-sealed pouches are
placed in a water bath at a precisely controlled temperature. Students
who successfully complete the course will be able to harness their
knowledge of the biochemical interactions and thermal dynamics that
underly the sous vide technique to achieve optimal flavor profiles and
textural nuances. Successful students will also be able to demonstrate
their understanding of the historical progression and contemporary
adaptations of sous vide technology, engage with state-of-the-art sous
vide equipment, and critically evaluate the applications of the sous
vide technique in haute cuisine.
Prerequisites: CULN 110 (Foundational Culinary Arts) and CULN 153
(Introduction to Gastronomic Science). Enrollment is limited to
Culinary Arts advanced track students.
Department: Culinary Arts
Schedule: MWF 2–5 P.M. Credits: Three (3)
Instructor: Marie Dubois, Certified Master Chef'),
