    ('reading-rdl-b1cc2c11741b6cc934d9ad00', 'Which of the following is the most accurate summary of the film review? 23. Which of the following is the most accurate summary of the film review? The film is visually uninteresting because of its muted palette. The film''s strong points are its character portrayal and cinematography. The film is likely to become a blockbuster. The film succeeds at portraying the economic issues confronted by artists. According to the review, the film might not appeal to audiences for which of the following reasons? 24. According to the review, the film might not appeal to audiences for which of the following reasons? Its slow pace Its lack of authenticity Its focus on the art world Lemoine''s acting style What does the review suggest about Marc? 25. What does the review suggest about Marc? He wants to help Elise resolve her struggles with painting. He is in Montclair to photograph Elise for a magazine. He is trying to deceive Elise. He is a better artist than Elise is. The Artisan’s Palette
Playing now as part of the university’s international film festival,
The Artisan’s Palette offers a contemplative alternative to
blockbuster spectacle.
Set in Montclair, France—a beautiful village marked by economic
decline—the film follows Elise Dupont, a painter confronting
creative stagnation. Her struggle intensifies with the arrival of Marc,
a self-described photographer whose shadowy motives become
apparent even as he strives to earn Elise’s trust.
Themes of authenticity and deception permeate the narrative,
underscored by striking cinematography that contrasts the vivid
colors of Elise’s canvases with the muted tones of her daily life.
While deliberate pacing and occasional narrative drift may
challenge viewers accustomed to rapid action, the film excels in
character depth.
Isabelle Laurent delivers a nuanced portrayal of Elise, balancing
vulnerability and resolve, while Jean-Pierre Lemoine’s enigmatic
Marc sustains tension throughout. For audiences drawn to
character-driven storytelling and visual artistry, this work offers a
richly textured exploration of ambition and identity.'),
    ('reading-rdl-b1e54a91a4ba8fad57f672dd', 'What is the main problem that Colin expresses about the assignment? 25. What is the main problem that Colin expresses about the assignment? He believes the topic is unimportant. He finds the topic too general to approach easily. He does not understand the assignment. He believes that the prompt makes false assumptions. What does Priya suggest is the purpose of the assignment? 26. What does Priya suggest is the purpose of the assignment? To summarize existing research on remote learning To criticize existing research on remote learning To choose a viewpoint and support it with arguments To analyze one’s personal experience with online courses What does Colin struggle with when reviewing the research? 27. What does Colin struggle with when reviewing the research? It discusses too many topics. It contradicts his own experience. It relies too heavily on theory. It is intended for experts only. Colin (8:20 P.M.):
I’m still wrestling with this week’s assignment. I get
it that we have to evaluate the longterm implications
of remote learning, but that feels incredibly broad.
Priya (8:22 P.M.):
I had the same reaction. I think the goal is to
show we can take a position and use evidence
to back it up, not cover every possible angle.
Mateo (8:26 P.M.):
Agreed. I’m focusing on how online courses affect
students’ motivation over time. There’s plenty of
research, but the findings contradict each other,
which makes the analysis tricky.
Colin (8:29 P.M.):
Exactly. Every article I read raises a
different concern—participation, cognitive
load, course design. It’s hard to figure out
which thread to prioritize.
Priya (8:31 P.M.):
I’d pick the one you can argue most clearly. The
professor said clarity matters more than trying to
sound “comprehensive.”'),
    ('reading-rdl-b217520f801a5096a9de00dc', 'What was the main purpose of the meeting? 23. What was the main purpose of the meeting? To select leaders for the Cultural Festival To finalize the date of the Cultural Festival To discuss preparations and funding for the Cultural Festival To review advertisements for the Cultural Festival What can be inferred about the Cultural Festival? 24. What can be inferred about the Cultural Festival? It needs additional volunteers. It is a monthly event. It is funded by alumni donations. It will include faculty participation. Student Council Meeting: March 10.
