    ('reading-rdl-c3025fabafad73a733e78fdc', 'What does the email suggest about the announcement of Maya''s training shift and orientation? 23. What does the email suggest about the announcement of Maya''s training shift and orientation? She was warned that the events were going to run longer than planned. She learned about the events from the student who was going to lead them. She was informed about the events when she accepted the job last week. She received very little advance notice about the timing of the events. What does Maya intend to do if she is granted an extension? 24. What does Maya intend to do if she is granted an extension? Ensure that her essay meets the stated criteria Devote the weekend to revising her essay Completely revise her essay''s argument Include more citations in her essay What does Maya offer to do? 25. What does Maya offer to do? Get help from the staff at the writing center Talk about her essay with Professor Alvarez Ask her library supervisor to call Professor Alvarez Join a study group for peer review of her essay From: maya11@rowancourt.edu
Subject: Request for an extension on Essay 2
Dear Professor Alvarez,
I’m writing to ask for a brief extension on Essay 2, which is due
Thursday at noon. My campus job in the library scheduled a
mandatory training shift last night and an additional orientation this
evening. The change was posted yesterday afternoon, and I
couldn’t move it. At this point, I’ve drafted about 60 percent of
the essay. I still need time to finish the analysis and revise the
citations.
Would it be possible to submit the essay by Friday at 5:00 P.M.
instead? I want to make sure it meets the rubric requirements for
organization and evidence. I can also stop by during your office
hours on Wednesday afternoon if you’d like to discuss my progress.
If an extension isn’t possible, I’ll submit what I have by the original
deadline. Thank you for considering my request.
Best,
Maya'),
    ('reading-rdl-c51947ee8d9fb0773388263f', 'Which statement best captures what the notice expects residents to do? 21. Which statement best captures what the notice expects residents to do? Follow quiet hour rules and keep noise low in shared and private spaces Use a new complaint procedure to report loud neighbors Attend a floor meeting to plan university-sponsored weekend activities Vote on changes to the university’s student housing contract Which situation would result in a violation under this policy? 22. Which situation would result in a violation under this policy? Talking softly with friends in the hallway at 9:50 P.M. on Tuesday Playing a movie at normal volume in the lounge at 1:10 A.M. on Saturday Listening to quiet music alone in a room at 11:30 P.M. on Friday Using a meditation app in a room with headphones at 10:05 P.M. on Sunday Dormitory Quiet Hours
On Sundays through Thursdays, quiet hours begin at 10:00 P.M.
On Fridays and Saturdays, they begin at midnight.
• Please limit noise in hallways, lounges, and rooms.
• Keep music and conversations at a low volume.
Violations will incur a $50 fine.
Contact Residence Life at 863-555-0153 with questions
or concerns.'),
    ('reading-rdl-c537b58566699097cf39eed3', 'What can be inferred about the Campus Connections program discussed in paragraph 1? 23. What can be inferred about the Campus Connections program discussed in paragraph 1? It is designed exclusively for first-year students adjusting to campus life. It replaced an earlier program that offered fewer than 100 clubs. It requires students to commit to at least one club per semester. It encompasses a broad range of student interests and activities. What is the primary purpose of the themed residence halls mentioned in paragraph 2? 24. What is the primary purpose of the themed residence halls mentioned in paragraph 2? To provide affordable housing options for students with limited financial resources To encourage interaction among students who have similar priorities and beliefs To separate students by academic major to enhance collaborative learning To reduce the administrative burden on the college-housing office The article suggests all of the following about the new initiatives EXCEPT: 25. The article suggests all of the following about the new initiatives EXCEPT: They involve collaboration with organizations outside Elmbrook College. They provide opportunities for students to align volunteer work with their academic interests. They give students access to graduate-level seminars and workshops. They offer benefits that extend beyond the students'' time at the college. BOOSTING CAMPUS LIFE:
NEW INITIATIVES FOR STUDENT ENGAGEMENT
Elmbrook College has launched several initiatives to enhance student
engagement this fall. The Campus Connections program now offers
over 100 clubs and organizations, ranging from environmental activism
to tech innovation. Students can explore diverse interests and build
communities around shared passions.
The revamped student-housing system features themed residence halls,
including Sustainability House and Global Cultures House, designed to
foster deeper connections among residents with similar values.
These learning communities encourage collaboration beyond the
classroom. The Career Center has partnered with local businesses to
create 300 part-time job opportunities for students. Additionally, the
Volunteer Hub platform matches students with community-service
projects aligned with their interests and academic goals.
“These programs will significantly enrich campus life and support our
students’ personal and professional growth,” said College President
Dr. Emily Caldwell. The initiatives aim to prepare students for success
during and after graduation.'),
    ('reading-rdl-c6d5ca9eb20452938644c348', 'What can be concluded from the form about Jennifer Liu''s project? 21. What can be concluded from the form about Jennifer Liu''s project? It involves collaboration with other students. It is required in order for her to graduate. It is related to non-academic work. It includes a video presentation. What is required for Jennifer Liu''s request to be completed? 22. What is required for Jennifer Liu''s request to be completed? She must provide the names of all those attending. She must finalize the reservation by sending a message. She must describe the project she intends to complete. She must agree to provide any equipment required by her group. Library Study Room Request Form
