    ('reading-rdl-d7e4ab4e0023faf73d44533a', 'Which statement best describes how the course grade is determined? 25. Which statement best describes how the course grade is determined? Performance on a small number of exams determines the course grade. The research proposal is weighted the same as the final project. Various assignments culminating in a final project contribute to the course grade. The course grade depends largely on peer feedback. According to the syllabus, why is it important that students not miss class? 26. According to the syllabus, why is it important that students not miss class? The course includes graded exams that cannot be retaken. Students must be in the classroom for access to the course folder. The instructor limits access to course materials after two absences. The quality of sessions depends on interaction among students. According to the syllabus, which action would violate course policy? 27. According to the syllabus, which action would violate course policy? Saving recordings in the course folder Using AI tools for brainstorming without noting their use Recording an interview after obtaining written consent Missing two class sessions of the course ANTH 214:
Qualitative Research Practicum (mini-syllabus)
Instructor:
Dr. Khatri
Office hours:
by appointment (in person or video)
Course focus:
Students practice interviewing, observation, and
ethical documentation while partnering with the
Campus Food Pantry to improve volunteer training.
Grading
(percentage of
final grade):
• Participation and lab notes: 30%
• Midterm (research design review): 30%
• Research proposal: 10%
• Final project-portfolio (including interview
transcript excerpts): 30%
Key policies:
• Attendance: Because peer feedback is critical to
each session, more than two absences may reduce
the final grade.
