    ('reading-rdl-e86f14f23f34ef4011fe3f95', 'Which person is eligible to attend and has done what is required before coming? 23. Which person is eligible to attend and has done what is required before coming? A member of the public who has completed a placement survey A currently enrolled student who has signed up on the listed website An undergraduate student who has emailed the Writing Center to reserve a seat A member of the faculty or staff who has signed up through the advising office All of the following are mentioned as topics covered in the workshop EXCEPT 24. All of the following are mentioned as topics covered in the workshop EXCEPT recording information prioritizing tasks test readiness critical thinking What will each participant take away from the workshop? 25. What will each participant take away from the workshop? An internship application An appointment with a tutor A customized learning plan A designated peer mentor Study Smarter: Academic Success Workshop
Unlock your best semester with a hands-on workshop designed to
elevate your study techniques.
In 60 minutes, we''ll cover proven strategies to give you a boost,
including effective time management, efficient note-taking, active
recall, interval-based study, and strategic exam preparation. You''ll
practice building a weekly learning plan, breaking down large
assignments, and tracking progress with simple tools.
We''ll also highlight campus resources—including tutoring, the
Writing Center, advising, and peer mentoring—so you''ll know
exactly where to get support when you need it. Bring your syllabi
and a laptop or notebook; you''ll leave with a personalized study
plan you can start using immediately.
• Open to all registered students—undergraduate & graduate
• September 10, 7:00 P.M.-8:00 P.M.
