    ('reading-rdl-ee5ee566c93478bba85e5d67', 'The main purpose of the email message is to 23. The main purpose of the email message is to ask about requirements pertaining to independent studies express appreciation to a professor for a course that Alyssa took in the past ask a faculty member for guidance on a research project explain why Alyssa wishes that more classes were offered on a particular novelist Alyssa mentions the length of three of George Eliot’s novels primarily to 24. Alyssa mentions the length of three of George Eliot’s novels primarily to explain why it may be difficult to complete an assignment she is currently working on cite a reason why there are no courses being offered that assign these novels emphasize that these novels will provide plenty of material for a proposed paper address potential concerns about whether she can finish the reading for a project on time The email indicates which of the following about Alyssa? 25. The email indicates which of the following about Alyssa? She has read some biographies of George Eliot. She has completed independent research for credit in the past. She has previously taken a course taught by Professor Stoll. She was referred to Professor Stoll by another faculty member. From:
avelina@rowancourt.edu
Subject:
Greetings from an Eliot fan
Dear Professor Stoll,
I am seeking a sponsor for an independent study next semester. I propose
to read three of George Eliot''s novels and write a paper focusing on Eliot''s
treatment of social class.
I became intrigued by Eliot when I read her novel Middlemarch in your
Victorian Literature course and wanted to explore Eliot''s work further.
Since no courses offered this year include her novels, I can only pursue
this project as an independent study.
The novels I propose to read are Adam Bede, The Mill on the Floss, and
Daniel Deronda. These are extremely long novels, but l am confident that
I can complete the reading in one semester. I will also read critical essays
on these novels and reviews of them that appeared during Eliot''s lifetime.
Please let me know if you would be willing to sponsor this project.
Regards,
Alyssa Avelin'),
