    ('reading-rdl-ef86a875d24c8b3c678c2990', 'The article suggests that the upcoming Iyengar yoga classes 23. The article suggests that the upcoming Iyengar yoga classes may be taught by more than one instructor during the semester can be taken by students of varying physical abilities will have both morning and evening sessions will earn course credits for students who wish to become yoga teachers The article implies which of the following about Iyengar yoga? 24. The article implies which of the following about Iyengar yoga? It is an older form of yoga than vinyasa. It is rarely taught outside of India. It puts more emphasis on philosophical readings than on physical practice. Its teachers are expected to have excellent pedagogical skills. The article mentions “flow yoga” primarily to 25. The article mentions “flow yoga” primarily to distinguish one style of yoga from another explain why it is a popular form of yoga comment on the subject of a yoga class taught in the previous semester emphasize the Campus Fitness Center’s varied offerings NEXT SEMESTER, THE CAMPUS FITNESS CENTER WILL OFFER
A SERIES OF RECREATIONAL CLASSES IN IYENGAR YOGA.
Iyengar yoga is distinct from other forms of yoga familiar to many
people. Various forms of vinyasa—“flow yoga” —are popular today.
If you have taken yoga classes, you have probably experienced this
approach, which involves moving from pose to pose with minimal
pauses. Iyengar yoga takes a more deliberate approach: Teachers
demonstrate poses, emphasizing alignment and precision, and then
instruct students with clear, specific language.
Developed by B.K.S. Iyengar (1918–2014), Iyengar Yoga is grounded
in the ancient Indian tradition and philosophy of Patanjali’s
Yoga-sutras. A master teacher himself, Iyengar became a highly
influential teacher of teachers, creating a rigorous system of training
and certification. Iyengar teachers are skilled in helping students
develop strength, flexibility, and concentration. Their approach
provides a safe way to learn yoga poses and accommodates students
with physical limitations.
Introduction to Iyengar Yoga: Tues/Thurs 5:00 P.M.–6:30 P.M.'),
    ('reading-rdl-f0ef795d88d5fdd7368f2d97', 'What is the main purpose of the announcement? 25. What is the main purpose of the announcement? To introduce a course that has not been taught before To encourage students to attend an English Department event To demonstrate the high quality of the Creative Writing program To ask for contributions to the Creative Writing Quarterly journal Which of the following would most likely NOT be a major focus of the seminar? 26. Which of the following would most likely NOT be a major focus of the seminar? Making a list of plot elements for use in fiction writing Writing drafts of conversations between characters Developing arguments to respond to prompts Reading a section of one’s own work to class members To register for the Creative Writing seminar, a student must 27. To register for the Creative Writing seminar, a student must submit a writing sample for evaluation have completed one introductory Creative Writing or English course be a first-year student be pursuing a degree in Creative Writing New Winter Term Writing Seminar
