Ben Alesten (5:01 P.M.)
Fingers crossed we can get in! But first things first; I’ll write to my advisor!'),
    ('reading-rdl-f776913db0be9454639b9aa2', 'Where can students check out and return books during the renovation? 23. Where can students check out and return books during the renovation? In the Main Building In the Meyer Student Union Building In the Frankson Library On the Main Quad What does the notice imply about the university’s digital resources? 24. What does the notice imply about the university’s digital resources? They can be accessed only during the temporary library’s operating hours. They may compensate for reduced convenience during the renovation. They were developed specifically in response to the renovation project. They will be accessible only to students who register through the online portal. What can be inferred from the notice about the Meyer Student Union Building? 25. What can be inferred from the notice about the Meyer Student Union Building? It is not close to the university’s Main Building. It is the only campus building large enough to house library services. It is not within easy walking distance of the Main Quad. It does not normally offer study spaces for students. Frankson Library Renovation and
Temporary Relocation
Attention University Community:
Beginning October 10, the Frankson Library will undergo a major
renovation to enhance study spaces and technological resources.
The project is scheduled to continue through March 15.
During this period, the library''s operational services will be
temporarily relocated to the second and third floors of the Meyer
Student Union Building. The temporary library spaces will operate
weekdays from 8:00 A.M. to 10:00 P.M. and on weekends from
10:00 A.M. to 6:00 P.M.
Library administrative offices will be temporarily relocated to the
university''s Main Building.
Extra shuttle buses will run between the Main Quad and the
Meyer Student Union Building to accommodate increased traffic.
Students are encouraged to explore our expanded digital resources
available through the university''s online portal.
We appreciate your patience as we improve our facilities.
For updates, visit the library''s webpage or contact
library@university.edu.'),
    ('reading-rdl-f819c5907ab5746b21bccaef', 'The purpose of the notice is to 23. The purpose of the notice is to offer recommendations describe a treatment advertise a product explain a process What can be inferred from the notice? 24. What can be inferred from the notice? The Campus Health Services office is open 24 hours a day to provide medical care. There have been more cases of flu on campus during the current year than in the previous year. Campus Health Services doctors do not prescribe antiviral medication to all flu patients. The symptoms of the flu are quite different from those of other respiratory infections. The notice mentions all of the following EXCEPT 25. The notice mentions all of the following EXCEPT symptoms that are common to both colds and flu measures people can take to protect their health where students can get a flu vaccination how to make an appointment at Campus Health Services Stay Healthy During
+
Cold And Flu Season
Cases of flu have been climbing this winter, and the Campus Health
Services office is advising all students, faculty, and staff to take
precautions.
Campus Health Services offers free flu vaccinations and
recommends that everyone except those with vaccine allergies come
to get the quick and effective shot.
In addition, measures like handwashing can make a big difference
in reducing your exposure to the flu virus. And of course, if you
feel sick, avoid close contact with others to keep from spreading
your illness.
Flu symptoms include fever, aches, sore throat, and fatigue.
While these symptoms are also typical of the common cold, the flu
tends to come on quite rapidly and symptoms can be severe.
Students experiencing these symptoms should see one of the Health
Services doctors as soon as possible. In some cases, antiviral
medication may be prescribed.'),
    ('reading-rdl-fe74dc0c18abd375a63d21f4', 'The article suggests that Coach Okoye 28. The article suggests that Coach Okoye began coaching the team a few weeks ago had won a title as a player previously coached at Ridgefield College once served as the team''s captain The article mentions all of the following EXCEPT 29. The article mentions all of the following EXCEPT the score of the match against Ridgefield College the date of the championship match how students can gain admission to the championship match the name of Baker''s opponent in the championship match The article indicates that fans attending the pep rally will be able to 30. The article indicates that fans attending the pep rally will be able to purchase tickets to the championship match watch the team practice obtain free items tour Springfield Stadium The Baker University women’s rugby team will play in
